e ports connecting to each other and to hosts h1 and h5. The packet and byte counts seem low, and current bit rates are zero, indicating low or no heavy traffic during the sampling.\n\nThe direct link between s1 and s5 used by h1-to-h5 traffic appears healthy and lightly loaded recently.\n\nTo better understand the slow transfer issue, I recommend running a TCP throughput test (iperf) from h1 to h5 to measure actual transfer bandwidth and identify any throughput bottlenecks. Would you like me to run this test? If yes, please specify the test duration (1-5 seconds).",
